258
00:20:22,798 --> 00:20:29,540
No matter what large language model you're using, if you don't have the proper prompt structure, you're not going to get the best results.

259
00:20:30,062 --> 00:20:35,364
So I'm going to briefly share with you the bulletproof prompting sequence that we teach to all of our students.

260
00:20:35,662 --> 00:20:41,552
Because if you have generic prompts, you're going to get generic answers. You're going to get the same answers that everyone else does.

261
00:20:41,710 --> 00:20:44,032
So I'm going to share this prompting sequence with you.

262
00:20:44,206 --> 00:20:49,552
And then I'll show you the results of a generic prompt versus the results of a prompt that actually does well.

263
00:20:49,934 --> 00:20:52,356
So let's jump into the bulletproof prompting sequence.

264
00:20:52,672 --> 00:21:00,164
And this is an acronym that we like to call GCAO or goal, context, action, and then output format.

265
00:21:00,494 --> 00:21:02,352
Here's an example of a good prompt.

266
00:21:02,542 --> 00:21:06,980
So it says, My goal is to create YouTube videos that will perform well for my channel.

267
00:21:07,278 --> 00:21:10,820
The analytics from my past videos are attached as context.

268
00:21:11,214 --> 00:21:19,460
I want you to analyze my past video stats from my channel, then research my niche and share three videos that would perform well for my channel

269
00:21:19,694 --> 00:21:23,492
based on current trends and what has worked for me in the past.

270
00:21:23,950 --> 00:21:31,952
Your final output should be a bullet list of those video ideas with title, length, target, and a brief summary of what that video should cover.

271
00:21:32,112 --> 00:21:38,512
And this is a good prompt because it has my goal, it has the context, it has the action that I want the model to perform.

272
00:21:38,672 --> 00:21:42,592
And then finally, it has the output format, how I want to see that finalized data.

273
00:21:42,830 --> 00:21:45,952
Do I want to see it in a bullet list? Do I want to see it in a table?

274
00:21:46,254 --> 00:21:48,192
Do I want an interactive diagram?

275
00:21:48,462 --> 00:21:49,552
That's what I'm defining there.

276
00:21:49,742 --> 00:21:52,612
So, first let's test out a generic prompt in Claude.

277
00:21:52,752 --> 00:21:56,912
I'm just going to say, I want you to give me ideas to grow my YouTube channel.

278
00:21:57,134 --> 00:21:58,340
And then I can send that off.

279
00:21:58,542 --> 00:22:02,672
And this is a short generic prompt, and it's going to give me a generic answer.

